## B.5 ❌ Content defects found

**D1 (P1) — `‖·‖_N` is used but never defined.** The macro `\wn` = ‖·‖_N appears in both bad-set definitions (§3.2 and §4.2): `B = {k ∈ Z_N : (n+1)‖v_p k‖_N < N}`. Under the intended reading ‖x‖_N = dist(x, Nℤ) this is correct — but the standalone paper **never defines it**, and a reader who assumes ‖·‖ = distance-to-nearest-integer gets ‖v_p k‖ = 0 and a vacuous definition. **Add one line to §2.1.**

**D2 (P1) — bad-set index range contradicts the equality theorem.** §3.2 indexes `p ∉ {u,w}` (**n−2** sets); §4.2 says "**n−1** bad sets"; Theorem 4.1 defines τ with `p ∈ [n]\{w}` (**n−1** runners). Since v_u ≡ −v_w (mod N) gives B_u = B_w, dropping *both* removes a set that matters. §3.2 must be `p ∈ [n]\{w}`. Also §4.2 reuses `w` as the running runner index — rename to `p`.

**D3 (P1) — the Eulerian formula is convention-dependent and, under the standard convention, wrong.** §2.3 states `h*(z) = Σ_k e_k (1−z)^{d−k} A_k(z)`. With classical Eulerian polynomials (A₁=1, A₂=1+z) this yields **10+z+z²** for n=3, not the table's (correct) **1+7z+4z²**. It is right only under Beck–Robins' shifted convention A₀=1, A₁=z, A₂=z+z². **State the convention explicitly** (one clause), otherwise the displayed formula contradicts the table it generates.

**D4 (P1) — stale text in Appendix B.1.** "A one-line reproduction of the **headline witnesses**…" is followed by the **superseded** 97/288 point. The headline is 16/47. Replace with the c(35) or the 1175-ths check (both already in Appendix C).

**D5 (P1) — broken hyperlink.** The Tao blog URL is split across two `\url{}` commands; the second (`a-remark-on-the-lonely-runner-conjecture`) is a relative, dead link. Use a single `\url{…}` and let `hyperref`/`url` break it.

**D6 (P1, high priority) — the LRC status claim contradicts its own citations.** §1.1: *"It is proved for at most seven runners… for eight through fifteen runners only computational verifications of special families are known."* But the bibliography cites, by title, **"The lonely runner conjecture holds for eight runners"** (2025), **"Nine and ten lonely runners"** (2025), **"Eleven, twelve, and thirteen lonely runners"** (2026), **"Fourteen and fifteen lonely runners"** (2026) — and §1.3 calls them "the rung results … are untouched". Either the status sentence is stale, or the citations are misdescribed. **This must be reconciled before submission**; I cannot verify the preprints without external lookup.

**D7 (P1) — Conjecture A.1 may already be a theorem, and is mis-stated.**
- *Mis-statement:* "the h*-polynomial of the **arithmetic matroid** of any projected basis `π([0,1]^n) ∩ Λ`". An arithmetic matroid has a **Tutte** polynomial, not an h*; and `π([0,1]^n) ∩ Λ` is a finite point set, not the zonotope. It should read "the h*-polynomial of the LR-zonotope Z(V)".
- *Priority:* real-rootedness of **lattice-zonotope** h*-polynomials is, to my recollection, addressed in the literature — specifically **Beck, Jochemko & McCullough, "h*-polynomials of zonotopes" (Trans. AMS, ~2019)**. If their theorem covers this class, the paper's "residual question of independent interest" is **not open**. This is the single highest-value literature check in the paper. I flag it as *requires verification*, not as established.

**D8 (P2) — decimal equality.** Table 2 writes `16/47=.3404` and `17/47=.3617`; these are truncations, use `≈`. (`29/80=.3625` and `1793/5000=.3586` are exact and fine.)

**D9 (P2) — sign-convention flip between hand checks.** Appendix C says "slopes **+3 and −5**" for the 1175-ths check but "slopes **−3 and +5**" for c(35) — same configuration type, opposite conventions. Fix one.

**D10 (P2) — "The The h*-polynomials are real-rooted"** (§3.5), duplicated word.

**D11 (P2) — undefined notation in Theorem 4.3.** Frontier cell `(1K, T−3U)`; hypotheses Hq±, H1g, H2r, H2m; and the k↔T map behind "95 < 244" in §3.4 (which T does k=2 correspond to?). As written, that comparison is not checkable.

**D12 (P2) — the m=9 row carries three different values.** Table 2: 1793/5000; §5.1 prose: a dyadic point at 0.358639…; Appendix B item 11: "clean witness **455/1269**" (≈0.358550) — a number that appears nowhere in the body. Order them explicitly in one footnote.

**D13 (P2) — bibliography ordering.** Declared "ordered by first citation", but `prog-artifacts` is cited before `Tao-blog`, and `Shephard` before `BeckRobins`. Also missing page numbers (Wills, d'Adderio–Moci, Rifford); **d'Adderio–Moci is dated 2014 — I believe the Advances paper is 2013**; and the Mirsky–Newman "see the account in Davenport–Rado, *Covering systems of negative congruences*, JLMS 38 (1963)" reference does not match the account I know (usually Erdős 1952 / Porubský–Schönheim). **Verify these two entries.**

